  "about": "A jazz ballad in F at 76, for the chord symbols: major and minor ninths, a thirteenth, and a secondary dominant with a flat nine (VIM7b9, D7b9, which pulls to the ii). The electric piano voices them without their roots, leaving those to the bass, and comps a different rhythm each pass (a variation picked in turn). Everything swings in triplets (0.667). The bass plays half notes under 0.5 and walks above it; past 0.55 the head gives way to a vibraphone solo in triplets, and past 0.7 an organ swells under it.",
